From: Tilo <tilo@tilo.so>
Subject: tpm: add a driver for the TPM behind Qualcomm mssecapp

Snapdragon X laptops that ship Microsoft Pluton as their TPM have no TPM
under Linux. Windows reaches it through ACPI TPM2 start method 14, served
by Qualcomm's QcTrEE and the qcom.tz.mssecapp Secure Application:

- mssecapp command 0x4007 reports its interface version and 0x4004 the
  physical address and size of a firmware-owned TCG CRB window: the
  control area followed by the command and response buffers.
- QcTrEE answers cmdReady and goIdle itself, by clearing the request bit
  in the control area, without calling into TrustZone.
- A CRB start is followed by command 0x4003, which runs the command in
  the window to completion before it returns.

Add tpm_qcom_mssec, a client of the mssecapp QSEECOM device that does the
same. It binds only when TrustZone reports a TPM type other than a
discrete or Qualcomm firmware TPM (those belong to qcom.tz.tpm), maps
only the window mssecapp names, and only when it is not system RAM, and
uses the buffers only when they lie inside it.

Snapdragon X suspends to idle, so no firmware sends TPM2_Startup on
resume; mark the chip firmware power managed so it is not sent
TPM2_Shutdown(STATE) either.

The protocol was taken from QcTrEE.sys and tpm.sys and matches the
independent analysis of the Surface Pro 11 Fedora project.

diff --git a/drivers/char/tpm/Kconfig b/drivers/char/tpm/Kconfig
index 8a8f692b6..3c93e1271 100644
--- a/drivers/char/tpm/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/char/tpm/Kconfig
@@ -220,6 +220,17 @@ config TCG_CRB
 	  from within Linux.  To compile this driver as a module, choose
 	  M here; the module will be called tpm_crb.
 
+config TCG_QCOM_MSSEC
+	tristate "TPM behind the Qualcomm mssecapp Secure Application"
+	depends on QCOM_QSEECOM
+	help
+	  Snapdragon X laptops that use Microsoft Pluton as their TPM reach it
+	  through a CRB window that the qcom.tz.mssecapp application in the
+	  Qualcomm Secure Execution Environment services. Say Yes here to make
+	  that TPM available, for example on the Lenovo Yoga Slim 7x.
+	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here; the module will
+	  be called tpm_qcom_mssec.
+
 config TCG_ARM_CRB_FFA
 	tristate "TPM CRB over Arm FF-A Transport"
 	depends on ARM_FFA_TRANSPORT && TCG_CRB
